From f7c3bd7b6caf8bad6ce1258970baeca5d860e6a6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AlexanderNyr <131390634+AlexanderNyr@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 17:21:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] PERF P1: profile-guided 8-byte RAM read fast path
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Five O2 gprof boot runs showed mem_read 313,666,250 calls / 45.66% of samples, with 235,535,030 calls from 8-byte page-table walks. Only full-span 8-byte little-endian RAM reads with A20 open now use unaligned-safe memcpy, after both ROM alias checks. MMIO, ROM, RAM boundary fill, closed A20, other widths and all writes use the old path.

Six bus vectors cover endian/unaligned, RAM end, ROM aliases and crossing, A20 masking, other widths, and MMIO-vs-RAM priority. One scratch-source NC swaps only the fast-path return endian; first vector asserts the exact LE value, binary RC=134, script RC=1, make RC=2. Post gprof: same 313,666,250 calls / 14.37% samples. Alternating pre/post triples on seven tapes kept identical work counts and yielded local paired time ratios 1.18–1.83x, with visible host variation: no fixed wall-time claim.

Measured: make test RC=0, make test-sanitize RC=0, make fuzz FUZZ_PROGRAMS=256 RC=0 (6,144 instructions all states match, zero host crashes), make bench BENCH_REPS=3 RC=0, four historical firmware/video stdout/log/PPM byte-identical. Frozen guest lanes SKIP without its build toolchain. See PERF_PLAN.md and same-phase CHANGELOG, ROADMAP, STATUS.
